/// Laurel SVGs embedded as string constants. We used to ship them as
/// `Bundle.module` resources via `Sources/StorescreensCore/Resources/`,
/// but Homebrew's keg-link mechanism does not symlink directories under
/// `bin/` into the prefix. The SwiftPM-generated Bundle.module accessor
/// looks for `storescreens-cli_StorescreensCore.bundle` next to the
/// executable at runtime, which on Homebrew installs is the symlinked
/// `/opt/homebrew/bin/`. Without the directory symlink, laurel rendering
/// crashed with "could not load resource bundle".
///
/// Embedding the two SVGs (about 6 KB each) eliminates the bundle entirely:
/// the SVG bytes ride inside the binary, OverlayPlacer renders them via
/// `NSImage(data:)`, and there is nothing for the OS to resolve at install
/// time. Source of truth for tweaks is still this file.
